//
// A single-column design whose memtile slave rules overlap, so packet id 14 is
// claimed by the id-10 rule. aiecc must reject it rather than emit a binary that
// misroutes on hardware. README.md records the measured hardware behaviour from
// before the rule set was rejected, and how to reproduce it.
//
// REQUIRES: peano
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu1_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: not %aiecc --get-xclbin --get-npu-insts --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin ./aie_arch.mlir 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: 'aie.rule' op is shadowed for packet id 10
